WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.480
777th All-Night Endless Chitty Chitty Gaming Tournament

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.220
Sorry, Nanana-chan, but can I sleep now?

00:00:16.150 --> 00:00:17.690
You're silly, Juugo.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.700
If you sleep, it's not an all-nighter.

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.590
Yeah, um... I know I'm 
the one who suggested it,

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.080
but I'm at my limit...

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:27.040
All right, let's get a move on.

00:02:31.970 --> 00:02:33.170
Good morning.

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:37.740
<b><u>Episode 8</u></b>

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:37.740
A Strange Visitor

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:34.950
Good morning!

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:38.100
Good... morning...

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:41.030
Tensai-san, there's a 
first-year here to see you.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.970
Oh. Thank you, Yumeji-dono.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.890
I wonder if she knows her.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.100
Everything's going great here.

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.290
Her? A first-year?

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.020
Well, about that...

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.070
That's surprising...

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.110
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:07.910
What was that about?

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:11.720
What's up?

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.380
I'm leaving.

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.330
What?

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:15.730
I'm going home!

00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.630
What are you talking about?

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.590
Who was that? What did she give you?

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.260
Huh? You want it? It's yours!

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:23.800
Hey, Tensai!

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:25.930
Wait, Tensai!

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.860
Tensai, come on!

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.820
<i>I don't get her...</i>

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.340
So, this is our new transfer student,

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.190
Tsujimi.

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:37.150
Another one?

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:37.850
Guy or girl?

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.740
Sensei, is he hot?

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:42.230
I'm Tsujimi Tetsunoshin. Pleased to meet you.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:42.820
Hey! Tetsu-kun!

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.560
Yama Juugo?

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.080
Why are you here?

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.620
Oh, you two know each other?

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.160
I wasn't informed of this, Sister...

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.040
Why don't you sit next to Yama, then?

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.330
I refuse!

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.150
Well, ready to go, Tsujimi-kun?

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.150
Please, lead the way.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.300
Showing him around the school?
 I'll join you!

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:11.170
Really, Tetsu-kun.
 I can't let you get ahead of me.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.940
I'm glad I don't get along with you.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:16.810
You two <i>are</i> friends, right?

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:24.840
I told you to leave me alone, jerk!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.320
Now, hold on!

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.490
That hurts!

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.010
Let go of me!

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:30.660
Huh?

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.380
What is that you're wearing?

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.350
That's Yun-chan... isn't it?

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.500
Whoa, wait!
 What are you doing, Tetsu-kun?!

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.210
Yama-kun?!

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:40.840
Don't worry. I'm tough!

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:42.710
Yama-kun!

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:47.680
<i>Damn... I didn't think he'd 
snap like that over Yun-chan!</i>

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:49.850
Get away

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.000
from Yun!

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.020
That's a teacher!

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.560
What are you guys doing?!

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.610
<i>Later, it was revealed that he</i>

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.730
<i>was just warning Yun-chan 
about her uniform.</i>

00:05:03.730 --> 00:05:05.510
<i>Tetsu-kun and I got in big trouble.</i>

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:06.950
<i>What does this have to do with me?</i>

00:05:07.690 --> 00:05:08.660
Sorry!

00:05:09.070 --> 00:05:10.890
Nah, it's fine.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.470
Yumeji-san, sorry we scared you like that.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:14.520
Sorry!

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.920
Oh, no, I'm fine.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.290
So you're a student here, Yun-chan?

00:05:20.740 --> 00:05:23.170
I had no idea the
 delivery boy was my senpai.

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:24.820
Delivery boy?

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.380
U-Uh...

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.010
That's my code name.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:30.970
Oh...

00:05:31.820 --> 00:05:34.960
Well, for the record, I'm Yama Juugo.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.670
I'm Saki! Yoshino Saki!

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:39.940
It's a pleasure!

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:43.510
Why do they call you "Yun"?

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:48.520
Sister told me I look like 
a Yun, so my name is Yun!

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:49.870
What the heck...

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.620
Oh. If the delivery
 boy is my senpai, then...

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.040
I'll have to call you 
Yama-senpai from now on, huh?

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:58.710
<i>Yama-senpai!</i>

00:05:58.710 --> 00:05:59.670
<i>Yama-senpai!</i>

00:05:59.670 --> 00:06:00.630
<i>Yama-senpai!</i>

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.380
Senpa—

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:06.580
Well, we'll look forward 
to seeing you around,

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.340
Yama-senpai.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:12.810
Are the second-years absent today?

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.890
Yes. Yama-kun contacted me earlier.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:17.490
That's perfect.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.650
I want to ask you something, Isshin.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:23.750
Why did you try to get a jump on

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.400
Yama-kouhai and the others?

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:30.120
I understand why you did what 
you did at the Rising Building.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:31.280
I even helped you.

00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.480
But what you did at the hot springs ruins

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:35.620
was not what we discussed.

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:37.830
What are you trying to say?

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.350
Wasn't joining forces with Yama-kouhai

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:43.000
and the others an option from the start?

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:47.220
What do you two think of the second-years?

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:48.980
What do you mean?

00:06:50.170 --> 00:06:54.100
Why are they searching 
for Nanana's Collection?

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:57.100
Though Nanana's Collection 
includes many treasures,

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.990
few grant the wishes of the owner.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:03.550
"The last one standing takes them all.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:08.610
It all comes down to whether
 you can get the treasures or not."

00:07:09.590 --> 00:07:12.450
Those are the words of a man I hated...

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:14.770
And they

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:18.040
may not have been entirely incorrect.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:23.360
Does that make Ibara and me your enemies?

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:26.900
That could never happen.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:31.930
I trust Tsurezure Kagetora and Ibara Yuu.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:35.610
Then why don't you trust the younger members?

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:37.220
They're in the Adventure Club, too.

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:40.390
Yes, and they are all brilliant.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.000
Far more than I am.

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:47.020
I'll be going now.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:54.820
Maybe he feels under pressure.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:56.950
What pressure?

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:02.510
He had to part with the Wizard's 
Cane that he desired for so long.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:04.560
Then the ruckus with the hot spring's fake...

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:06.960
It must all be having an effect on him.

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:09.690
Maybe.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.470
Hey, is this the original Adventure Club?

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:20.060
The one in the middle 
is Konjou-senpai, right?

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.460
This one is Sanada Fumika.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:27.020
The one next to Isshin is Fuwa,
 who quit last year after being injured.

00:08:27.960 --> 00:08:30.380
Wow, they're all pretty well-known.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:32.400
Isn't this one...

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.830
Ikusaba-senpai?

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:39.970
Yeah. But I haven't heard
 much about him that's good.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:44.210
I'm a little worried about Tensai-chan.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.830
I still don't understand her.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.260
Oh, are you the one
 who's living here now?

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:00.860
Sorry. Looks like I startled you.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:03.100
Who the hell are you?!

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.560
Hey, don't be so alarmed.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:09.010
I just have something to discuss with her.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:15.990
It's been a long time, Nanana.

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:18.700
Why did you come here, Hiiyo?

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.200
Why else would I come here... but this?

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.230
Um...

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:28.750
Oh, I'm Ikusaba Hiiyo.

00:09:29.090 --> 00:09:32.120
As you can see,
 I'm gathering Nanana's Collection.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:35.340
That's the Rain Bell.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.750
It's officially called the 
"Angelus of Heaven's Rain."

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:42.510
If you ring it while praying, 
it brings rain clouds.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.770
What are its weaknesses?

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:47.280
It can be manipulated by 
the strength of the wish,

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:50.370
and it won't work in the same location twice.

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:51.290
Also...

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.570
I've heard enough.

00:09:53.530 --> 00:09:55.250
So it's just garbage, then.

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:05.870
Time's up, huh?

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.760
Ikusaba!

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:14.380
Are you okay, Nanana?

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:15.710
Uh-huh.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:19.180
Pay your rent!

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:28.270
Hey, Juugo...

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.270
Would you buy me some pudding?

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:35.200
Huh? Er... right now?

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.780
Yeah. A good kind, if you can.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:40.030
Please?

00:10:42.260 --> 00:10:43.180
Okay.

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:53.300
Stop pestering me.

00:10:53.300 --> 00:10:55.340
I have nothing to say to you.

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:58.720
I wouldn't either,
 if you'd just pay your rent!

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.080
I have no reason to pay rent to you.

00:11:14.420 --> 00:11:15.810
I don't see why

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.900
I have to put up with
 this over your silly rent.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.860
You know that's not all.

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.750
Jumping around like that helps
 spread alcohol through your system.

00:11:22.750 --> 00:11:24.950
You'll trip over your own feet and fall.

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:27.780
Thanks for the concern.

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:31.870
See? You can't even stand anymore.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.910
As I told you before,

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:38.640
I don't agree with your
 arbitrary decision to end my contract,

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:41.120
so I have no intention of 
paying the remaining rent.

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:42.090
You...

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.370
Hold it! Ikusaba!

00:11:46.020 --> 00:11:47.470
Damn it!

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.380
Shiki-san!

00:11:54.400 --> 00:11:56.350
Oh, Juugo.

00:11:56.350 --> 00:11:58.520
You're stumbling around...

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.070
You've had too much to drink.

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.140
And what brings you out here?

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:04.730
Nanana-chan asked me to buy pudding.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.430
And I came to look for you on the way.

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:08.840
I see.

00:12:09.230 --> 00:12:11.350
I think I'll buy some beer, too.

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:18.910
Um... is Ikusaba-san a former 
resident of the Happy House?

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:20.170
Yep.

00:12:20.690 --> 00:12:22.550
And he wouldn't pay his rent?

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:24.130
That's right.

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:28.420
Um... were he and Nanana-chan...

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.310
Ikusaba Hiiyo

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:37.190
was the one who lived in Room 202 before you.

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.000
But he never even went near the room,

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.610
and he totally neglected Nanana!

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:48.850
Here's your pudding.

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:52.540
He called it garbage.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:56.250
There were people

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:59.820
who once thanked me because of that bell.

00:13:00.290 --> 00:13:01.680
I was so happy.

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:03.720
I see...

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:06.340
So it's just garbage, then.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.210
Why do you look like that?

00:13:11.340 --> 00:13:13.300
What did I look like?

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:16.980
You looked sad, and in pain.

00:13:17.410 --> 00:13:19.820
Oh, and that fake
 laugh made you look ugly.

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:23.640
Not really. I was kidding.

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:25.780
Thanks for the pudding.

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:30.370
It's a good kind...

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.080
I don't know...

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:36.860
Maybe things won't go 
as I'd hoped, after all.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.220
Like what?

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:41.220
I mean the powers of Nanana's Collection

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:44.960
won't always go to the
 people I want them to.

00:13:44.960 --> 00:13:48.780
I knew Hiiyo had no need for the Rain Bell,

00:13:48.780 --> 00:13:51.560
but when I'm asked, I have to answer.

00:13:51.770 --> 00:13:54.060
If you don't want to,
 can't you just refuse to tell?

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.070
I can't.

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:57.350
These are the rules I decided on.

00:13:57.880 --> 00:14:00.450
If I can't even follow my own rules,

00:14:00.450 --> 00:14:02.780
there's no point in me being me.

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:05.490
In you being you?

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.450
Everyone has things only they can do, right?

00:14:09.920 --> 00:14:12.390
It doesn't have to be something big.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:15.180
But I feel like, if I can see it through,

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:19.420
I'll be able to think there 
was meaning in me being me.

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:23.400
So I won't lose to my own 
decisions, no matter what.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.560
That's the proof that I'm me.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:33.350
But even though I think 
I'm doing the right thing,

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:37.810
there are times when I
 wonder if that's really true.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:43.270
<i>Am I trying to find Nanana's 
Collection for Nanana-chan's sake?</i>

00:14:44.270 --> 00:14:45.180
<i>But...</i>

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:48.780
<i>"Just garbage." "Useless."</i>

00:14:49.290 --> 00:14:51.230
<i>I've had those thoughts, too.</i>

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:54.280
<i>Just like the guy who
 treated Nanana-chan like that.</i>

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:55.450
<b>Konjou Kasumi</b>

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:56.750
<b>So, you who came after me,
 please save my best friend.</b>

00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:59.620
<i>So it's possible that
 message wasn't originally for me,</i>

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.840
<i>but for Ikusaba-san?</i>

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.170
<i>Not for me?</i>

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:09.880
<i>No... I have to do it!</i>

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:14.850
<i>But what does it really mean</i>

00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:18.540
<i>to save Nanana-chan?</i>

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:24.650
Thanks for waiting, Tetsu!

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.920
Well, ready to go home, Tetsu-kun?

00:15:29.310 --> 00:15:30.610
We can have some fun on the way!

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.450
Yama Juugo! I have no
 intention of befriending you!

00:15:35.490 --> 00:15:37.540
You shouldn't say things like that.

00:15:37.540 --> 00:15:40.000
It's more fun if we're all together!

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:47.150
Bears! Bears! Look, bears!

00:15:44.580 --> 00:15:47.560
So did you come to this school 
to look out for Yun-chan?

00:15:47.860 --> 00:15:48.880
Maybe.

00:15:49.840 --> 00:15:51.280
Your Sister's orders?

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:53.170
Who knows?

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:55.270
Or for Nanana's Collection?

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:57.410
What did you say?

00:15:57.410 --> 00:15:59.270
Not a thing.

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:01.360
I'm gonna get some tokens.

00:16:02.190 --> 00:16:05.650
<b>Token
 Exchange</b>

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.980
Oh, you're...

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:10.830
Hello.

00:16:14.320 --> 00:16:17.220
You're the guy from Nanana's room... Uh...

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:18.620
Yama Juugo.

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:23.620
Yama-kun, why do you live 
in that weird, haunted room?

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:27.090
Because it's an awesome place to live.

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:29.800
Glad to hear it.

00:16:32.060 --> 00:16:33.810
Do you like this sort of thing?

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.300
Yeah. I learn a lot from this.

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:38.030
You learn from this?

00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:41.110
Games like these allow more

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:43.830
opportunities for player 
involvement than other games.

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:46.310
That's what I think, as do the others.

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:48.270
Others?

00:16:48.560 --> 00:16:50.800
You might call it strategizing.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:56.190
How will one player's actions 
affect the course of the game?

00:16:56.190 --> 00:17:01.200
What actions should you take 
to achieve the greatest profit?

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:06.040
You think about that while
 watching all the people around you?

00:17:06.580 --> 00:17:07.960
Yes, I do.

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:13.970
That's a lot of effort for just a game.

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:15.880
That's a narrow outlook.

00:17:16.290 --> 00:17:19.850
Yama-kun, do you prefer winning or losing?

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:21.600
Winning, of course.

00:17:23.530 --> 00:17:26.230
I feel the same way.
 So does everyone else.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:30.420
So what type of person do you
 think is left standing in the end?

00:17:30.420 --> 00:17:32.360
The strong ones, I guess?

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.320
Strong in what way?

00:17:33.450 --> 00:17:34.810
Physical.

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:39.410
There's also intelligence, information, 
luck, and countless other factors.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:43.620
But I believe there's one
 thing that's absolutely essential.

00:17:44.130 --> 00:17:45.320
What's that?

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:47.370
Refusal to compromise.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.310
"It's too much work."

00:17:49.310 --> 00:17:51.090
"There's no point in going that far."

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.790
People who think such things will lose.

00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:59.050
So, um... what exactly is it
 that you learn here, Ikusaba-san?

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:02.390
In a word... humanity.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.730
All right!

00:18:05.650 --> 00:18:07.780
Well, I guess I'll be going.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.730
I lost ten thousand.

00:18:11.080 --> 00:18:12.010
Huh?!

00:18:12.760 --> 00:18:15.560
Be honest. What did you think just now?

00:18:16.050 --> 00:18:20.760
Well... I thought that's pathetic,
 after all that exposition.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.370
That's what you learned today.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.620
So this is where you were, Yama-senpai!

00:18:31.890 --> 00:18:33.170
Hi there.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:35.130
H-Hello.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:38.130
What's your name?

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:41.140
Y-Yoshino Saki.

00:18:42.340 --> 00:18:44.080
I'm Ikusaba Hiiyo.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:46.210
Nice to meet you.

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:48.140
You introduced yourself properly. Good.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:50.700
You're getting awfully familiar.

00:18:50.700 --> 00:18:52.900
Don't get so upset, boyfriend-kun.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:55.690
No girl will ever like a stiff.

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.570
I'm not her boyfriend.

00:18:57.980 --> 00:18:59.610
Later, kiddos.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:04.260
Yun-chan, are you okay?

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:05.830
She's fine.

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:09.210
She just has a mild fear of men.

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.070
Hey.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:16.760
Are you the club president now, Four-eyes?

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:18.470
Ikusaba-san?

00:19:19.140 --> 00:19:20.980
What brings you here?

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:23.600
I was just feeling a little nostalgic.

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.730
At least serve me tea, Four-eyes.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:32.020
Oh... I'm sorry.

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:33.820
Please.

00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:36.480
Are there other members?

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:39.110
Six, including myself.

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:41.200
That's quite the group.

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:44.210
Yes, more than when you were a member.

00:19:44.210 --> 00:19:47.680
You've learned to say some 
interesting things, Four-eyes.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:49.910
So, got anything to show for it?

00:19:50.170 --> 00:19:52.120
I'll leave that to your imagination.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.710
You're awfully impudent, Four-eyes.

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.210
Why don't I crush you right here and now?

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:03.020
I'm kidding.

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:06.220
There's no need to go that 
far against the likes of you.

00:20:08.080 --> 00:20:10.460
Still taking care of that Nanana's Collection

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:13.220
treasure Kasumi gave you, Four-eyes?

00:20:13.670 --> 00:20:15.010
I am.

00:20:15.010 --> 00:20:17.440
It's a memory of the original Adventure Club.

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:21.150
Really? I sold mine off ages ago.

00:20:21.420 --> 00:20:22.570
You...

00:20:23.130 --> 00:20:25.710
Useless garbage should be disposed of.

00:20:25.710 --> 00:20:27.330
That's how I work.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.870
You're wrong!

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.220
Four-eyes.

00:20:31.630 --> 00:20:33.490
The words you're spitting out

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:36.600
and the way you still waste time in this room

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:38.710
are mere imitations of someone else.

00:20:39.100 --> 00:20:42.420
I feel nothing whatsoever 
for a phony like you.

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:44.660
Don't come skulking around me

00:20:44.660 --> 00:20:47.180
with your irritating little game of house.

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:49.770
Thanks for the tea.

00:20:53.050 --> 00:20:55.310
I couldn't say anything, again.

00:20:58.600 --> 00:21:00.330
Kagetora, are you there?

00:21:00.330 --> 00:21:01.190
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:03.940
Follow Ikusaba-san.

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:06.780
I suspect he's plotting
 something that involves the school.

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:09.510
<i>Understood. I'll look into it.</i>

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:11.320
Kagetora...

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:12.450
<i>What?</i>

00:21:12.870 --> 00:21:15.890
Do not fight him. If he spots you, run.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:19.680
That man, Ikusaba Hiiyo,

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:22.390
was the most proficient
 of all the original members

00:21:22.390 --> 00:21:24.480
in the use of Nanana's Collection.
